to promote human flourishing, a technology to learn the fundamental skills of well-being. That's really what they're intended for. Of all these meditation practices you describe, mindfulness is probably one many of our listeners would be familiar with. Why has mindfulness meditation in particular become so well known? I think mindfulness meditation has become so well known in part for historical reasons. It was one of the first forms of traditional Asian-style meditation that was taught in the West. Also, John Cabot-Zinn, a very dear friend and colleague, developed a standardized instruction called Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction that has been taught at academic medical centers throughout the U.S. and in most parts of the Western world.
旨在促进人类的蓬勃发展，这是一项学习幸福之基本技能的技术。这确实是它们的初衷。在您描述的所有这些冥想实践中，正念可能是我们的许多听众都熟悉的一种。为什么正念冥想尤其变得如此广为人知？我认为正念冥想之所以变得如此广为人知，部分原因是历史原因。它是西方教授的早期传统亚洲风格冥想形式之一。此外，我的挚友兼同事约翰·卡巴金（Jon Kabat-Zinn）开发了一套名为“正念减压疗法”的标准化教学法，该疗法已在美国各地的学术医疗中心以及西方世界的大多数地区得到教授。

8
