And this is a very convenient form of mindfulness meditation that is packaged in a very standardized format and can be taught very easily. And this has helped to, I think, increase the availability and therefore the popularity of mindfulness-based practices. You've practiced meditation yourself since the 1970s when you were in grad school. and you've written about how it's always been an important part of your life. But it wasn't part of your academic research for the first couple of decades in your career. And I understand it was actually the Dalai Lama who inspired your research in this area. Can you talk, tell us that story? Certainly I'd be happy to.
这是一种非常方便的正念冥想形式，采用高度标准化的包装，可以非常容易地教授。我认为这有助于提高正念实践的可及性，进而提升其受欢迎程度。您自己从20世纪70年代读研究生起就开始实践冥想了，

