large areas of the brain in those specific regions. They don't. There's no evidence to show that they do. And so it may well be. that there are curvilinear relationships that are very complex and so when we're first learning some of these skills for example the skills of self-regulation certain areas of the prefrontal cortex which are important for this may become enlarged but then after they become more automatic after these skills are learned at a more at a greater level of expertise it may be be that these areas of the brain begin to recede back to what they were. And so it's,
巨大。他们并没有。没有证据表明他们有这样的情况。所以很可能存在着非常复杂的非线性关系，因此当我们刚开始学习其中的一些技能时，例如自我调节的技能，对此很重要的前额叶皮层的某些区域可能会变大；但随后，在它们变得更加自动化之后，在这些技能以更高的专业水平被掌握之后，大脑的这些区域可能开始回缩到它们原本的大小。所以，

